179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 110 0 R
/T (DDS and agencies defined by the law as Employers must check the registry prior to employing a care provider. For purposes of the DPPC Abuser Registry, Employer means any agency that provides services or treatment to people with I/DD pursuant to a contract or agreement with DDS; funding administered by DDS; or a license issued by DDS. The DPPC Abuser Registry is not a public registry. By law, the DPPC Abuser Registry can only be accessed by DDS or Employers who are funded by, contract with, or are licensed by DDS. Employers are required to create verified accounts to check whether prospective care providers are on the DPPC Abuser Registry.)
/E (DDS and agencies defined by the law as Employers must check the registry prior to employing a care provider. For purposes of the DPPC Abuser Registry, Employer means any agency that provides services or treatment to people with I/DD pursuant to a contract or agreement with DDS; funding administered by DDS; or a license issued by DDS. The DPPC Abuser Registry is not a public registry. By law, the DPPC Abuser Registry can only be accessed by DDS or Employers who are funded by, contract with, or are licensed by DDS. Employers are required to create verified accounts to check whether prospective care providers are on the DPPC Abuser Registry.)
